Here's a quick update on the ENTS automation work:

Playwright migration: The ENTS test cases are being moved from Selenium to Playwright BDD Cucumber. The feature files, step texts and object repository keys stay the same, so existing scenarios run unchanged from the Test Runner, and the setup stays Docker-ready.
Runtime test data: Herds no longer need to be hard-coded. Each run pulls fresh transferor and transferee herds from the ENTS Oracle database. Before using a herd, the framework checks it in the portal (blacklisted, missing or expired) and picks a new one if it fails. Used herds are tracked so they aren't picked twice.
Test case status: TC_01 and TC_02 are migrated. TC_03 (cross-agent transfers) passes for its first two sections. The third section is blocked on test data: some herds returned for one agent don't show in that agent's Transfer Out list, and I'm investigating this with a DB check. I've also added handling for transferee searches that return more than one match, so the current holder (no end date) is selected.
Appeals and Staff: Appeals automation is complete. Staff automation is in progress.

Next steps: Resolve the TC_03 data issue, tighten the submission success check, and continue with Staff.

